      "message": "I think that would fix the current issue, now I\u0027m having trouble passing the tcpmv2 fuzz test.\n\nBut, tcpm_set_vconn is only really called from set_vconn, so I don\u0027t think what you\u0027re proposing is that different from what we have now. I don\u0027t have a strong opinion. It seems a bit cleaner since then we don\u0027t have to independently manage tcpmv1 and v2.\n\nIs there any reason we would need to enable vconn before enabling SOP\u0027? If so we might need to keep it how it is now, what you\u0027re proposing would move the SOP\u0027 enable prior to the PPC VCONN enable (which I guess it was before disabling TCPC VCONN anyway).",
